WEBVTT

00:00:24.400 --> 00:00:26.560
What should I do?

00:02:00.450 --> 00:02:03.120
Oh, he's up. Tohru's up!

00:02:03.330 --> 00:02:07.750
Castaway: The Other World

00:02:03.500 --> 00:02:06.040
Big sister, he woke up!

00:02:06.040 --> 00:02:08.500
All right, I'll be right there!

00:02:17.840 --> 00:02:19.050
You're...

00:02:19.470 --> 00:02:23.140
We don't need introductions, right?
How are you feeling?

00:02:24.600 --> 00:02:26.060
Tohru Kazasumi...

00:02:26.770 --> 00:02:28.600
That's right, isn't it?

00:02:31.440 --> 00:02:34.230
Hey, did you cut your hair?

00:02:36.030 --> 00:02:37.950
I guess I wanted
to try something different.

00:02:37.950 --> 00:02:39.490
Those are weird clothes!

00:02:40.240 --> 00:02:41.950
But it looks cool!

00:02:42.830 --> 00:02:43.740
Thanks.

00:02:44.490 --> 00:02:48.960
Tohru, Tohru... Ma-chan and the others
were snacking on the food in the fields!

00:02:48.960 --> 00:02:51.250
Come on! It was just one tomato!

00:02:51.250 --> 00:02:53.040
It's not good to snack when you're working.

00:02:53.750 --> 00:02:55.920
You should make sure to apologize.

00:02:55.920 --> 00:02:58.050
Big sister was scolding him earlier!

00:03:04.890 --> 00:03:06.850
We're here. This is it.

00:03:07.770 --> 00:03:09.810
This is our home.

00:03:10.770 --> 00:03:13.900
Welcome to the hideout of Team Bastian.

00:03:15.610 --> 00:03:18.320
Thanks for helping to carry stuff.

00:03:18.320 --> 00:03:20.320
No, it's the least I could do.

00:03:20.320 --> 00:03:22.870
Well, just sit anywhere you like.

00:03:23.280 --> 00:03:24.120
Sure...

00:03:25.580 --> 00:03:28.200
Since I was in the fields,
I have mud all over me.

00:03:28.200 --> 00:03:29.410
Hold on a second.

00:03:33.420 --> 00:03:37.420
So your side is called the 17th Far East
Imperial City Management District.

00:03:37.420 --> 00:03:39.300
That sounds like a tongue-twister.

00:03:40.930 --> 00:03:42.550
Where is this?

00:03:42.550 --> 00:03:45.970
The same place. What used to be Japan.

00:03:45.970 --> 00:03:48.270
It's called Frontier Stratos.

00:03:49.520 --> 00:03:50.770
And the kids?

00:03:51.770 --> 00:03:55.400
Those are the kids we live with. They're orphans.

00:03:55.650 --> 00:04:00.320
Tohru, I mean, our Tohru,
brings them in from all over the place.

00:04:00.700 --> 00:04:01.820
He does?

00:04:02.280 --> 00:04:07.370
He lost his parents early in life,
so they probably remind him of himself.

00:04:07.620 --> 00:04:08.830
I see...

00:04:16.090 --> 00:04:17.130
Remy...

00:04:22.340 --> 00:04:23.180
What's wrong?

00:04:23.180 --> 00:04:25.430
Well, um... uh...

00:04:27.310 --> 00:04:28.560
You've never seen them?

00:04:28.560 --> 00:04:29.640
I haven't!

00:04:37.980 --> 00:04:40.030
Why didn't you shoot me?

00:04:41.400 --> 00:04:43.490
You're right. Why didn't I?

00:04:44.490 --> 00:04:48.240
It's true that I wanted to talk to you some time.

00:04:48.540 --> 00:04:53.620
If I wasn't in the middle of battle, I'd never want to kill anybody.

00:04:55.080 --> 00:04:58.040
Me too, yeah...

00:04:58.550 --> 00:05:01.130
Okay, you can turn around.

00:05:01.130 --> 00:05:04.800
Tohru Kazasumi from
the 17th Something Management District.

00:05:14.730 --> 00:05:20.030
When I saw you talking to those kids,
I thought to myself, "Tohru is Tohru, after all."

00:05:22.400 --> 00:05:28.830
But if Tohru, my Tohru, was here right now,
I don't think he'd hesitate to shoot you.

00:05:30.830 --> 00:05:32.290
I'm sure you're right.

00:05:32.830 --> 00:05:36.250
Even if it was the me from your side.

00:05:41.300 --> 00:05:46.220
All right, we're going to step out for a bit,
so hold down the fort and take care of them, okay?

00:05:46.220 --> 00:05:47.340
Got it!

00:05:47.340 --> 00:05:49.510
Going on a date with big brother Tohru?

00:05:50.140 --> 00:05:51.260
Are you jealous?

00:05:51.260 --> 00:05:53.930
That's so nice! I want to go, too!

00:05:53.930 --> 00:05:56.100
Nope. You have to stay home.

00:05:57.020 --> 00:05:58.310
No choice, huh?

00:05:59.520 --> 00:06:01.780
I wonder if this is cheating?

00:06:02.030 --> 00:06:03.900
Take care!

00:06:15.710 --> 00:06:18.540
You said "take care of them"... 
do you have someone who's sick?

00:06:19.250 --> 00:06:22.840
Well, not right now.
There's someone that got a bit injured.

00:06:23.960 --> 00:06:26.800
Don't worry, it's not any of the children.

00:06:30.390 --> 00:06:30.930
What?

00:06:31.390 --> 00:06:33.970
We're supposed to be enemies, right?

00:06:33.970 --> 00:06:36.730
But we're worried about illness and injuries.

00:06:36.890 --> 00:06:38.060
Is that strange?

00:06:38.060 --> 00:06:40.770
Nope, it's not strange at all.

00:06:44.730 --> 00:06:47.650
It's Tohru after all.
You would have traits like that.

00:06:47.650 --> 00:06:50.070
It's not strange, not strange at all.

00:06:55.450 --> 00:06:57.660
Wait, when I came here,
this place was...

00:06:57.660 --> 00:07:02.500
At full tide, the seawater flows in
all the way up to this area.

00:07:03.290 --> 00:07:06.630
As time passes the scenery changes, huh?

00:07:07.340 --> 00:07:12.890
The world I was in, and this world...
maybe they were both originally the same place.

00:07:13.100 --> 00:07:15.350
That's kind of romantic.

00:07:15.890 --> 00:07:20.100
That guy... Tohru from this side...
aren't you worried about him?

00:07:20.480 --> 00:07:26.320
From the sound of it, he got sent to your—
what was it?— Management District.

00:07:26.320 --> 00:07:29.860
I don't know,
but that's the feeling I get.

00:07:29.860 --> 00:07:34.280
Well, if you're all right,
I'm sure he's all right, too.

00:07:35.160 --> 00:07:36.160
Just a guess, though.

00:07:36.870 --> 00:07:38.500
You have faith in him.

00:07:40.580 --> 00:07:42.080
He's my lover, after all.

00:07:42.540 --> 00:07:45.500
Um, can you keep stuff like that
between you and the other me?

00:07:47.010 --> 00:07:49.420
Since we don't know
when he'll come back,

00:07:49.420 --> 00:07:52.140
it's probably better for you
if you aren't at the hideout.

00:07:54.640 --> 00:07:55.560
Come on, let's go!

00:07:56.260 --> 00:07:58.390
You want to know more 
about our side, don't you?

00:08:03.270 --> 00:08:05.150
Every building is in ruins.

00:08:05.150 --> 00:08:10.490
About 100 years ago, all sorts of things
like war and earthquakes happened.

00:08:10.490 --> 00:08:12.740
The country called Japan ceased to exist.

00:08:12.740 --> 00:08:14.910
We had something similar happen to us.

00:08:14.910 --> 00:08:18.200
There are places here and there
that are still in some semblance of working order,

00:08:18.200 --> 00:08:20.750
but most places look like this.

00:08:20.750 --> 00:08:22.500
What about the government?

00:08:22.500 --> 00:08:24.420
There are things like village assemblies

00:08:24.710 --> 00:08:28.550
where the survivors gather together
and try to make do.

00:08:28.550 --> 00:08:29.840
I see.

00:08:29.840 --> 00:08:33.840
But in order to survive around here,
in the end you have to form small groups,

00:08:33.840 --> 00:08:36.810
and somehow get by
with what you have.

00:08:36.970 --> 00:08:38.470
And that's what Bastian is?

00:08:38.470 --> 00:08:42.270
Yup. That's our team,
and Tohru is the leader.

00:08:42.270 --> 00:08:44.980
We're kind of like a local police force.

00:08:44.980 --> 00:08:48.150
But as you can see,
it's basically an orphanage.

00:08:48.400 --> 00:08:50.530
You don't receive any foreign aid?

00:08:50.690 --> 00:08:53.280
Frontier is pretty much isolated.

00:08:53.450 --> 00:08:55.490
We're self-sufficient, too.

00:08:55.700 --> 00:08:59.790
We farm and we fish.
Sometimes we go hunting, too.

00:09:00.450 --> 00:09:02.080
It must be tough.

00:09:02.080 --> 00:09:05.290
It's been like this ever since
 I was born, so I'm used to it.

00:09:06.840 --> 00:09:09.340
But everyone looks so alive.

00:09:09.800 --> 00:09:13.470
It's so different from our world
where corporations regulate our lives.

00:09:13.680 --> 00:09:15.010
Does it look that way to you?

00:09:15.010 --> 00:09:15.800
Yeah.

00:09:18.470 --> 00:09:21.600
We do have authorization
from the UN to rule ourselves.

00:09:21.600 --> 00:09:25.770
I heard our clan was in the center of it,
and there was a fierce debate.

00:09:26.270 --> 00:09:27.230
Clan?

00:09:27.230 --> 00:09:31.110
Yeah, the Katagiri Clan.
It doesn't exist on your side?

00:09:31.280 --> 00:09:31.820
Yeah.

00:09:33.950 --> 00:09:36.870
I wonder what Big Brother would've said
if he'd heard that.

00:09:38.200 --> 00:09:40.830
That's right.
The Kyohma on this side was...

00:09:41.660 --> 00:09:43.910
Forget I said anything!
Just forget it!

00:09:43.910 --> 00:09:46.170
Let's not talk about battles and stuff!

00:09:46.370 --> 00:09:48.460
But still... I'm sorry.

00:09:48.460 --> 00:09:50.300
Don't apologize!

00:09:50.300 --> 00:09:51.210
Umm...

00:09:52.130 --> 00:09:53.130
Sorry.

00:09:53.130 --> 00:09:54.300
Geez!

00:09:56.630 --> 00:09:59.600
I feel like I'm here with the old Tohru.

00:10:01.220 --> 00:10:01.810
Huh?

00:10:03.100 --> 00:10:04.180
What's wrong?

00:10:05.600 --> 00:10:10.110
This looks familiar.
There's probably a tree like this on our side, too.

00:10:10.110 --> 00:10:15.150
I see... so it looks different,
but there are parts that are still the same.

00:10:15.150 --> 00:10:15.650
Yeah.

00:10:18.700 --> 00:10:20.160
By the way, about earlier...

00:10:20.160 --> 00:10:23.240
In the photo frame, well,

00:10:23.240 --> 00:10:27.460
there was a picture of me from your side and 
Remy where they look like friends.

00:10:28.750 --> 00:10:30.590
Does he live with you guys?

00:10:34.260 --> 00:10:35.630
Actually...

00:10:36.130 --> 00:10:38.470
There's something I want to show you.

00:10:40.970 --> 00:10:44.430
Tohru's responses have completely disappeared.

00:10:44.640 --> 00:10:45.980
Not only from the present,

00:10:45.980 --> 00:10:49.230
but it seems he hasn't been transported
to Japan in 2015, either.

00:10:49.810 --> 00:10:52.360
I want a thoroughly detailed analysis of the logs
from when he disappeared.

00:10:52.360 --> 00:10:53.730
We're already on it!

00:10:53.730 --> 00:10:57.990
Hurry. This may perhaps be a possibility.

00:11:01.070 --> 00:11:04.490
<i>So their facilities are similar to our lab...</i>

00:11:13.670 --> 00:11:15.460
Their security is sparse.

00:11:23.680 --> 00:11:25.100
You again?

00:11:26.560 --> 00:11:28.940
Don't believe the Timekeepers.

00:11:29.100 --> 00:11:30.690
I don't believe them.

00:11:31.190 --> 00:11:34.650
But, that doesn't mean that I have 
any reason to believe you, either.

00:11:34.650 --> 00:11:38.360
Your voice, to me,
is the same as the Timekeepers.

00:11:38.360 --> 00:11:40.660
It's meaningless noise
with nothing to back it up.

00:11:53.000 --> 00:11:55.550
The lack of quality security is the same, too.

00:11:56.400 --> 00:11:59.690
<b>Degradation
 Remy Odhner</b>

00:12:10.060 --> 00:12:11.020
We're here.

00:12:11.480 --> 00:12:12.520
What's this?

00:12:13.150 --> 00:12:16.440
Remy was one of us, too.

00:12:18.400 --> 00:12:22.240
I think he came roughly three years ago...

00:12:22.990 --> 00:12:28.080
He was with us for only a short time,
but he's a part of our family.

00:12:29.040 --> 00:12:31.120
He died in battle, I assume?

00:12:31.120 --> 00:12:32.040
Nope.

00:12:32.620 --> 00:12:37.500
He wasn't very physically strong to begin with,
but he succumbed to an illness.

00:12:38.880 --> 00:12:43.760
Tohru went to get some medicine,
but he didn't get back in time.

00:12:44.430 --> 00:12:45.800
It was just so sudden.

00:13:22.170 --> 00:13:28.810
He was a very shy boy, but had opened up to Tohru,
so it seemed like they were brothers.

00:13:29.060 --> 00:13:31.020
I see.

00:13:31.470 --> 00:13:35.400
I think it was around the time
that Tohru stopped smiling as much.

00:13:37.020 --> 00:13:41.610
This is a place where the children who died
before they could grow up are laid to rest.

00:13:44.200 --> 00:13:48.370
You just said that the people here looked so alive, but...

00:13:48.740 --> 00:13:52.830
But in this world where power is everything,
children who have no parents—

00:13:53.250 --> 00:13:58.500
no, even with parents,
it's very hard to live in a world like this.

00:13:58.750 --> 00:14:02.050
So he was trying to protect his family.

00:14:02.210 --> 00:14:04.470
Wherever you go in Frontier, it's like this.

00:14:05.010 --> 00:14:08.640
There are fewer doctors now than there used to be, too.

00:14:09.260 --> 00:14:11.680
We don't have nearly enough.

00:14:12.180 --> 00:14:18.690
But, since Tohru and I started joining the missions, life has gotten so much easier.

00:14:19.110 --> 00:14:24.610
We started getting food rations,
and we got medical facilities, too.

00:14:25.150 --> 00:14:28.870
I'm sorry. I was the one that said
we should stop talking about this.

00:14:34.370 --> 00:14:36.330
Thanks. You're so kind.

00:14:36.920 --> 00:14:38.580
That's not true.

00:14:39.000 --> 00:14:40.880
You're so kind, Tohru.

00:14:41.710 --> 00:14:43.000
You're so kind...

00:14:46.380 --> 00:14:49.260
Those that don't help out
won't get any dinner!

00:14:50.180 --> 00:14:51.100
Let's go!

00:14:51.100 --> 00:14:52.510
Wait up!

00:14:52.510 --> 00:14:55.810
He doesn't smile at all anymore.

00:14:56.390 --> 00:15:02.190
He pretends to act cheerful in front of the children,
but his heart is completely withered.

00:15:02.190 --> 00:15:04.860
He always looks like he's in a lot of pain.

00:15:05.360 --> 00:15:06.900
Kyoka...

00:15:07.780 --> 00:15:08.780
Right.

00:15:09.320 --> 00:15:13.080
When he says my name, he sounds just like that,
as if it was difficult to say.

00:15:13.660 --> 00:15:16.910
Hey, am I helping you like I should be?

00:15:18.920 --> 00:15:20.670
Come on, answer me.

00:15:21.710 --> 00:15:22.880
You...

00:15:24.550 --> 00:15:27.840
You always pestered me
when I was trying to be alone,

00:15:28.300 --> 00:15:29.720
and called out to me.

00:15:30.590 --> 00:15:34.560
But, deep down, I was 
really happy about it, Kyoka,

00:15:35.180 --> 00:15:39.730
that you took notice of someone like me,
and had expectations of what I could be.

00:15:39.730 --> 00:15:43.230
Can I continue to be at your side from now on?

00:15:44.980 --> 00:15:46.360
I would never say no.

00:15:48.320 --> 00:15:52.570
Thank you for always being at my... at his side.

00:15:57.000 --> 00:15:58.870
I hope you continue to in the future.

00:16:00.210 --> 00:16:04.420
You should say things like that
to the me on your side.

00:16:05.000 --> 00:16:06.420
How can you, of all people, say that?

00:16:06.420 --> 00:16:07.880
I mean...

00:16:14.970 --> 00:16:17.720
<i>Tohru! Tohru! Can you hear me!</i>

00:16:18.060 --> 00:16:19.390
Is that you, Kumi?

00:16:19.560 --> 00:16:22.190
<i>Oh, I'm so glad!
I finally got through to you!</i>

00:16:22.190 --> 00:16:23.860
<i>Are you all right, Tohru?</i>

00:16:23.860 --> 00:16:24.900
Well...

00:16:24.900 --> 00:16:27.070
<i>Data link establishment confirmed!</i>

00:16:27.070 --> 00:16:29.860
<i>I've identified the spacetime coordinates
of your current location, Tohru.</i>

00:16:29.860 --> 00:16:31.450
<i>I'll transfer you right away!</i>

00:16:31.450 --> 00:16:34.450
I'm sorry, Kumi,
please give me a little more time!

00:16:34.450 --> 00:16:37.040
<i>I don't know when the link will break.</i>

00:16:37.040 --> 00:16:39.370
<i>Commencing forced transfer sequence!</i>

00:16:41.120 --> 00:16:43.250
<i>Nothing unusual on the biological scans.</i>

00:16:43.710 --> 00:16:47.710
<i>Target NDSF detected.
Commencing brain-wave tracking.</i>

00:16:44.540 --> 00:16:45.420
Kyoka...

00:16:45.540 --> 00:16:49.300
It was nice to talk to you,
but when I see you next, we'll be enemies.

00:16:48.300 --> 00:16:52.760
<i>Anti-tachyon circuits booted.
Commencing weak boson propagation.</i>

00:16:49.920 --> 00:16:52.760
That may be the case, but...

00:16:53.390 --> 00:16:55.100
<i>Chrono potential is stable.</i>

00:16:55.550 --> 00:16:57.470
<i>Circuit has reached criticality.</i>

00:16:57.890 --> 00:17:00.060
<i>Creation of CP field confirmed.</i>

00:17:01.730 --> 00:17:03.400
<i>Time vault, release!</i>

00:17:05.810 --> 00:17:06.820
I'll see you again!

00:17:13.200 --> 00:17:16.620
Oh man, maybe it would have been better
if I hadn't met him.

00:17:19.830 --> 00:17:22.910
I wonder if this counts as cheating, too.

00:17:35.680 --> 00:17:37.010
<i>Big Brother Tohru!</i>

00:17:38.600 --> 00:17:39.430
Remy!

00:17:42.350 --> 00:17:43.230
Tohru?

00:17:47.150 --> 00:17:49.320
Get away! That's an intruder!

00:17:49.320 --> 00:17:53.570
Verification complete.
This is not the Tohru Kazasumi from this world.

00:17:53.570 --> 00:17:56.450
He is presumed to be an identical individual 
from another world.

00:17:56.450 --> 00:17:57.700
The other Tohru?

00:17:57.870 --> 00:17:59.280
Don't move from there.

00:18:00.200 --> 00:18:03.750
<i>Caution. Coercive transfer sequence underway.</i>

00:18:03.750 --> 00:18:05.420
<i>Materialization coordinates uncertain.</i>

00:18:17.180 --> 00:18:18.390
Kyoka!

00:18:18.640 --> 00:18:22.020
Kyoka! Kyoka! Kyoka!

00:18:27.100 --> 00:18:27.980
Kyoka!

00:18:28.650 --> 00:18:29.060
Kumi!

00:18:29.310 --> 00:18:30.520
<i>Stop the machine!</i>

00:18:30.650 --> 00:18:32.940
No good! Someone's hacked it!

00:18:36.030 --> 00:18:36.950
Kyoka!

00:18:37.160 --> 00:18:39.160
Damn it, that bastard!

00:18:41.080 --> 00:18:42.080
Stop it, Remy!

00:18:42.200 --> 00:18:44.080
Shut up! Don't tell me what to do!

00:18:44.330 --> 00:18:45.040
Remy!

00:18:45.040 --> 00:18:46.790
Dammit! What should we do?

00:18:53.510 --> 00:18:55.340
I'll kill him myself!

00:18:56.470 --> 00:19:00.050
Open your eyes. Answer me, Kyoka!

00:19:00.550 --> 00:19:02.350
There's something I want to tell you.

00:19:02.680 --> 00:19:03.890
I want to be together again...

00:19:04.310 --> 00:19:06.060
Life signs confirmed.

00:19:06.230 --> 00:19:08.350
If we hurry with treatment,
we'll make it in time.

00:19:08.350 --> 00:19:10.860
Someone, please get a stretcher ready.

00:19:10.860 --> 00:19:12.980
We'll transfer her
to the emergency treatment room.

00:19:14.940 --> 00:19:21.570
Spacetime transfer from another world, and the transfer of an individual from another world to 2015...

00:19:21.870 --> 00:19:24.200
We now have the perfect data recorded!

00:19:24.200 --> 00:19:28.040
With this, even if we don't
have the backing of that stupid kid...

00:19:39.760 --> 00:19:43.260
It's useless, Remy.
You're only using up your own stamina.

00:19:43.260 --> 00:19:45.100
Don't get so friendly with me!

00:19:52.860 --> 00:19:54.190
An Energy Cube!

00:19:54.190 --> 00:19:57.490
I got a hold of this by killing one of your friends.

00:19:57.690 --> 00:20:00.780
I wonder what will happen
if I use this on myself?

00:20:00.780 --> 00:20:02.280
Stop! If you do that...

00:20:02.280 --> 00:20:04.330
I hate you!

00:20:19.510 --> 00:20:20.340
Tohru!

00:20:20.340 --> 00:20:21.090
Kazasumi!

00:20:21.090 --> 00:20:23.300
I don't need any of you!

00:20:25.310 --> 00:20:26.010
Dodge!

00:20:29.430 --> 00:20:33.230
I'll take everything away from you,
Tohru Kazasumi!

00:20:37.190 --> 00:20:39.570
Is that... Remy?

00:20:45.660 --> 00:20:46.950
This is an absolute mess.

00:20:50.160 --> 00:20:51.330
Matsurika!

00:20:53.120 --> 00:20:54.880
They're just like flies.

00:20:54.880 --> 00:20:57.380
This is what I should have done
from the beginning.

00:20:57.670 --> 00:20:59.880
That boy used a Cube on himself.

00:21:00.050 --> 00:21:00.970
We have to stop him!

00:21:00.970 --> 00:21:01.760
I'll assist you!

00:21:04.680 --> 00:21:06.890
What's this?

00:21:15.110 --> 00:21:17.270
So much power...

00:21:17.270 --> 00:21:18.270
We can't get close.

00:21:25.410 --> 00:21:26.700
Is that Degradation?

00:21:29.200 --> 00:21:30.040
Remy!

00:21:33.830 --> 00:21:35.920
This is earlier than planned.

00:21:36.500 --> 00:21:40.170
It's incomplete, but I suppose this will do.

00:21:52.180 --> 00:21:54.940
Now, this is the beginning...

00:23:25.440 --> 00:23:27.240
Dogma needs to live life
in a more fun way!

00:23:27.240 --> 00:23:28.410
I just want an easy life.

00:23:28.410 --> 00:23:29.780
Fun and easy are different!

00:23:29.780 --> 00:23:31.990
We're going to break the world apart
in a fun way!

00:23:31.990 --> 00:23:33.540
You don't have to tell me
in these previews...

00:23:33.540 --> 00:23:35.370
We'll make it more fun!

00:23:35.370 --> 00:23:37.460
We're just all over the place!

00:23:37.210 --> 00:23:39.920
<b><i>REUNITING </i></b>A BITTER DREAM

00:23:37.460 --> 00:23:38.640
Next episode: "Reuniting."

00:23:38.640 --> 00:23:39.750
"A Bitter Dream."
